Photorealistic vintage 1980s Japanese Hi-Fi medallion, square, straight-on, isolated on a pure flat black background, centered and filling 80 percent of the canvas. One circular object, half open-face reel-to-reel aluminum tape spool, half precision audio dial. Rim: diamond-cut brushed champagne silver aluminum with fine precision-machined degree notches around the circumference, and a continuous thin ring of glowing electric fluorescent teal VFD light inside it. Face: dark charcoal brushed aluminum turntable with fine concentric audio grooves and three precision-cut chrome reel spokes. On the face, two centered lines of lettering in crisp glowing retro fluorescent aqua lettering: first line "Killa", second line "YuE" (capital Y, lowercase u, capital E). Lettering very large and legible at tiny sizes. High-end Tokyo audiophile studio mood, crisp focus. No other objects, no extra text, no watermark.
